.TH FSLOOP 1
.SH NAME
fsloop \- use files while servers crash (a test)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsloop
.I dir rounds
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsloop
is a test of crash recovery: it keeps using files while the test kills
and restarts servers
.RB ( "make crash-test" ).
Each round writes a file in
.IR dir ,
commits it
.RB ( sync ),
reads it back and checks it, renames it and commits again. A round that
sees an error is done again: a sync says so when the file server
restarted since the last one. At the end every file is checked once
more, and it prints
.B "fsloop: N rounds, R redone, T ms, OK"
or what was wrong.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every file was right; 1 otherwise, or after too many errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crash (1),
.BR init (8),
.BR fs (4)
